# Tentative d10 Resolution

Raven's Heart is currently using a **Storyteller-style d10 dice pool** as its
tentative core randomizer while the resolution engine is tested.

This is a provisional implementation, not a locked final dice engine.

The provisional Attribute + Talent + Skill + Specialty composition uses **one applicable rating per category**; the Talent contribution only applies to one of its five governed Skills, and ungoverned Skills remain usable. See [[Attributes and Talents]].

A trait's rating is currently 0–25 and provides **one die for every full 5 rating levels**. On a real action, attribute-, Talent-, Skill- and Specialty-sourced dice are kept separate for XP purposes, even when added to the same resolution pool; see [[Use-Based Trait Advancement]].

## Dice Pool

Roll a number of d10s equal to the relevant rating or pool.

- 7, 8, or 9 = **1 success**
- 10 = **2 successes**
- lower results currently contribute no successes

The total number of successes is the roll's result.

A roll may produce **zero successes**. This is intentional, including on resource
Cost rolls.

## Application and Effect

Application rolls use their success total against **Complexity** or **Avoidance**.

Effect rolls use their success total as the magnitude applied against
**Recalcitrance** or **Resilience**. Personal resource tracks translate that
magnitude into graded marks according to [[Resource Tracks]].

**Meet it to beat it:** Application succeeds when Accuracy successes are **greater than or equal to** Complexity/Avoidance. Then roll Potence independently. A successfully applied Effect with any positive Potence successes gives at least **one Minor mark**; reaching the effective Recalcitrance/Resilience threshold gives **Middling**, twice gives **Major**, three times gives **Final**, and larger multiples give additional Final marks. Project **Scope** provides slots per grade, while personal resource **Resilience** provides personal track capacity. See [[Project Framework]] and [[Resource Tracks]].

Critical-success/failure predicates and equipment-specific defense/threshold adjustments remain open. The four **mark grades** are distinct from cross-scale **Tiers**.

## Tier

Scale differences are currently handled by [[Tentative Tier Scaling]].

The working model keeps ordinary dice pools bounded and converts a rolled result
into the Tier of its opposition by a factor of 10 per Tier of difference: divide
when rolling upward in Tier, multiply when rolling downward. Static opposition
stays at its own Tier. Exact Tier anchors and special exceptions remain
provisional.
